+ * it when the view moves. A shadow can therefore also carry the exact real
+ * value (`sc`) of the integer a register holds. It is created by a load from a
+ * registered trig table (the exact sine instead of its rounded Q8 entry) or
+ * combines with untracked integers, which are exact by themselves, through
+ * add / sub / constant shifts / mult / div. An SH of such a register into a
+ * packet turns it into that half's sub-pixel coordinate. The integer the guest
+ * computed is never changed; the consumer accepts a scalar-derived half when
+ * it lies within 2 px of the packet's integer (the truncations it replaces add
